    "id": "HIT-Owen/jingzhang-ai-corridor-regeneration",
    "slug": "jingzhang-ai-corridor-regeneration",
    "title": "京张信号带 THE SIGNAL CORRIDOR：让穿行于公共空间的AI服务亮起信号",
    "titleEn": "Jing-Zhang Signal Corridor (THE SIGNAL CORRIDOR): Requiring AI Services Traversing Public Space to Signal Their Status",
    "summary": "京张铁路用信号灯指挥列车进退，京张信号带用同一逻辑约束穿行于公共空间的AI服务：每个进入走廊的AI服务必须'发信号'——公开它做什么、用什么数据、谁负责、何时可停。一条9公里信号脊串联三座信号站（基准·发信·报信）与十二个信号点，把铁路遗产的行车纪律转译为AI治理的空间制度。全部空间建议基于临时边界，属概念建议，待正式数据发布后复算。",
    "summaryEn": "The Jing-Zhang Railway used signal lights to direct trains in and out; the Jing-Zhang Signal Corridor applies the same logic to constrain AI services traversing public space: every AI service entering the corridor must 'signal'—publicly disclosing what it does, what data it uses, who is responsible, and when it can be stopped. A 9-kilometer signal spine links three signal stations (Benchmark, Origin, and Public) and twelve signal points, translating the operational discipline of railway heritage into a spatial institution for AI governance. All spatial proposals are based on provisional boundaries and are conceptual suggestions, to be recalculated once official data is released.",
