    "title": "道岔·SWITCH 2.0——把京张 AI 创新带做成可暂停的公共试验线",
    "titleEn": "THE SWITCH 2.0 — A Pauseable Public Test Line for the Jing-Zhang AI Innovation Belt",
    "summary": "京张走廊不需要再增加一座孤立的 AI 园区，而需要一条能让实验进入日常、也能在公共利益受损时停下来的试验线。SWITCH 2.0 以一条南北公共主脊、三处重点工场、两条协同接口和四道放行门，把 12 个概念场景、5 项慢变量、18 项更新项目和 45 项可复算指标组织成一个可试、可审、可退的城市设计方案。所有空间边界仍为临时约束，全部实施内容均为概念建议。",
    "summaryEn": "The Jing-Zhang corridor does not need another isolated AI park. It needs a test line that lets experiments enter daily life and stop when public value is harmed. SWITCH 2.0 uses one north-south public spine, three working yards, two coordination sidings, and four release gates to connect 12 conceptual scenarios, five slow variables, 18 renewal projects, and 45 recalculable metrics into a testable, reviewable, and withdrawable urban-design proposal. All spatial boundaries remain provisional and all implementation content is conceptual.",
