    "titleEn": "The Pass Line / 京张放行线",
    "summary": "京张放行线主张：每一项 AI 服务进入街区前，必须先在实体空间里通过儿童、适老、无障碍与照护者四类使用场景的现场走测——不过门槛，不上街。方案把'放行'做成贯穿京张AI创新带的空间制度原型：三类放行门广场、三条标准走测线、四个重点区门型映射、五个验收子门与儿童友好作为放行前置，让 AI 治理从纸面承诺落到可走、可测、可纠错、可退出的街道现场。",
    "summaryEn": "The Pass Line argues: before any AI service may enter a street, it must first pass a live walk-test on site across four use scenarios — children, elderly, accessibility, and caregivers. No clearance, no street. The proposal turns 'clearing' into a spatial institution across the Jing-Zhang AI Innovation Belt: three pass-gate plazas, three standard walk-test routes, four key-area gate-type mappings, five verification sub-gates, and child-friendliness as a clearance precondition — turning AI governance from paper promises into walkable, testable, correctable, exitable street reality.",
