    "title": "双机京张 · DOUBLE HEADING——人机双机牵引的百年爬坡线",
    "titleEn": "DOUBLE HEADING · JINGZHANG — A Century-Old Climbing Method for the Human-AI City",
    "summary": "1909年，京张铁路用本务机车加补机的双机牵引爬上关沟三十三千分之一的陡坡；2026年，本方案把这套百年工法转译为AI创新带的城市总纲——人当本务机车，AI为补机，可加挂、可摘挂。方案提出一轴双机、三坡两翼、百点呼应的总体结构：牵引轴（京张遗址公园活力带）贯通南北，三处重点区读作三段创新爬坡（自主之坡·众智园、策源之坡·AI原点社区、转化之坡·大钟寺），12张呼应点场景卡、3处产业测试验证区、4座AI朝圣地标与机车铭牌荣誉体系落于31片全覆盖用地分区之上。全部空间建议均为概念建议，基于临时边界生成，官方红线公布后全链重算。",
    "summaryEn": "In 1909 the Jing-Zhang Railway climbed the 33-per-mille Guangou grade with double heading: a lead locomotive driven by people, a banking engine adding traction, coupled for the climb and uncoupled after it. This proposal translates that century-old method into the master principle of the Centennial Jing-Zhang AI Innovation Belt: humans drive, AI banks — attachable, detachable, always answerable. The plan proposes One Axis with Twin Systems, Three Slopes and Two Wings, and a hundred Call-and-Response nodes: 12 scenario cards, 3 industry test zones, 4 AI pilgrimage landmarks and a locomotive-nameplate honor system, all grounded on a 31-zone full-coverage land-use partition. Every spatial suggestion is a concept proposal generated on provisional boundaries; the full chain will be recalculated once official redlines are released.",
